  "summary": "I started software development 10 years ago from the web and mobile development and it helped me a lot to acquire enough knowledge about how the software works in harmony with hardware.\nNowadays, I am focusing on front-end development with Angular 2/4/5, React.js/Redux, Meteor, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, SCSS/SASS/LESS, ES6/7, TypeScript/JavaScript, jQuery, etc.\nMobile App development using the Ionic framework and React Native is one of my core skill and I have 8 years of experience in iOS and Android mobile app development using Ionic, React Native, Swift, Objective-C, Xamarin, and Meteor.\nAlso, I am quite familiar with back-end development and deployment with AWS (Lambda, DynamoDB, EC2, SNS, S3, Cognito, Elastic Beanstalk, etc), Firebase, Heroku, etc.\nI have rich experience in CMS website development with WordPress/Shopify and Drupal.\n\nHere are my skill sets.\n\n- Web development:\n✓ AngularJS (Angular js, 2, 4, 5), Angular Bootstrap, Angular Material \n✓ React.js, Redux/Flux/Mobx, Redux-Saga, React-Bootstrap/Material-UI/Toolbox   \n✓ Vue.js, Vuetify\n✓ Ruby on Rails \n✓ ES6/7, JavaScript/TypeScript, Meteor.js, HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap, SASS/SCSS/LESS \n✓ Meteor, MongoBD, Meteor-Blaze\n✓ CMS: Wordpress, Shopify, Keystone.js\n\n- Mobile App development:\n✓ Hybrid mobile: Ionic framework 1&2&3, React Native, Cordova/PhoneGap, Meteor, Kendo UI, AppPresser\n✓ Native mobile: Xamarin, Swift, Android Studio\n\n- Backend service and Database\n✓ Amazon S2, S3, EC2, Parse, back4app, Ruby on Rails, MongoDB, Firebase\n\n- Source Control: \n✓ Git, Github, Bitbucket, GitLab, BaseCamp, Trello, Jira, Asana\n\nBuilding long-term relationships with clients are the most important thing to me.\n\nI'm flexible with my working hours and always feel happy to collaborate with any freelancers you work with.\n\nBest Regards.\n\nOscar.",
